# Line endings, decided once so the suite is not red on one machine and green on
# the other.
#
# Everything here is read by bash and python on two machines: a Linux cloud
# container and Amanda's Windows box. Git ships core.autocrlf=true on Windows,
# which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. The blobs in this repo are LF, so that
# rewrite lands in the working tree only, and a gate then compares a value
# against the same value plus a trailing carriage return.
#
# On 2026-09-08 that failed the holiday-anchor test while printing
#     labor-day resolved 2026-09-07, wanted 2026-09-07
# because a carriage return only moves the cursor. Nine dates, every one of them
# correct, all reported as mismatches, and nothing on screen to say why.
#
# eol=lf pins the working tree to LF on every platform. Binaries are marked so
# nothing tries to translate them.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pyc   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
